IMPORT prelude

-- Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance) Act 2016 (ACT), with the Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance)
-- Regulation 2016 (ACT), which holds every dollar figure.
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the applicant", "the assisted person",
-- "the commissioner", "a primary victim", "a related victim", "a homicide witness". The applicant's questions are in
-- vocfa-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Part 2: s 7 (act of violence, by schedule 1), s 9 (injury), s 10 (homicide), s 11 (primary
-- victim), ss 12 to 15 (related victims, classes A, B and C), s 16 (homicide witness), s 17 (close family member), with
-- the dictionary's dependant, financially independent, relevant person, sexual offence, offence against the person and
-- schedule 1 offence. Part 3: ss 18 to 23 (eligibility), s 24 with reg s 5 (maximum total), s 26 with reg s 6 (immediate
-- need), s 27 with reg s 7 (economic loss), ss 28 to 30 with reg ss 8 to 10 (recognition payments), s 31 (application and
-- evidence), s 32 (time), s 33 (notice), s 45 (disqualifying circumstances, as findings), s 47 (reductions, as findings).
-- Part 4: ss 51 to 55 and s 60 with reg s 11 (funeral expense payment). Part 5: ss 62 and 64 to 67 (repayment).
-- Part 9: s 92 (2) and schedule 2 (the deadline for reconsideration). Part 10: s 96 with reg s 12 (lawyers' costs).
--
-- FIGURES. Regulation R11 (effective 1 July 2026). The s 25 CPI indexation (of the s 24, s 28, s 29 and s 30 amounts)
-- and the s 97 WPI indexation (of the s 96 amounts) are taken as already reflected in R11, which SL2026-8 amended for
-- 1 July 2026. No other year's figures are encoded.
--
-- NOT COVERED, each answering an explicit `not covered` value: recovery from the offender (pt 6), the victims financial
-- assistance levy (pt 7), administration and secrecy (pt 8), ACAT review procedure beyond the deadlines (pt 9),
-- applications for criminal injuries before 1 July 2016 (s 98), and the commissioner's guidelines (s 87, not deposited).
--
-- Edition: A2016-12, Republication No 10 (R10), effective 26 November 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/A2016-12.txt; SL2016-10, Republication No 11 (R11), effective 1 July 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../../victims-of-crime-financial-assistance-regulation-2016/registers/source-bundle/SL2016-10.txt.
-- © Australian Capital Territory, CC BY 4.0; see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance) Act 2016 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that reaches one of these answers with the reason, and a test asserts it.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 7 (1) (c), s 10 (1) (a): the Act's concepts start on its commencement; s 98 lets some earlier criminal injuries in
    `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
    `recovery from the offender (part 6) is not encoded`
    `the victims financial assistance levy on convicted offenders (part 7) is not encoded`
    `administration, the commissioner's functions and secrecy (part 8) are not encoded`
    `review by the ACAT (part 9, s 95): its procedure and time limit are in the ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2008, which is not deposited`
    `the commissioner's guidelines (s 87) are not deposited`

§§ `Dates`

-- Legislation history: "remainder commenced 1 July 2016 (s 2 (1) (a))".
`the commencement of the Act` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2016

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        `the year` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0
    AND (   (NOT (`the year` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR `the year` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

-- The same day and month, a number of years later. READING: 29 February, in a year with no 29 February, becomes
-- 28 February. Neither the Act nor the Regulation says; the Legislation Act 2001 (not deposited) governs periods.
GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years` `years after` `the day` MEANS
    IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
        AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
        AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `years`)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `years`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `years`)

GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days` `days after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `days`)

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE
      `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second`
    THEN `the first`
    ELSE `the second`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE
      `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or before` `the first` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

§ `Part 2 -- important concepts`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- the offences for an act of violence`

-- Schedule 1, division 1.2.1 (General offences) items 1 to 7, and division 1.2.2 (Family violence offences) items 1 to
-- 25 as one choice. s 7 (1) (b) (ii) also admits "an offence prescribed by regulation"; Regulation R11 prescribes none.
DECLARE `Associated offence` IS ONE OF
    -- div 1.2.1 item 1: Crimes Act, "an offence against pt 2", "offences against the person"
    `an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2`
    -- item 2: Crimes Act pt 3, "sexual offences"
    `a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3`
    -- item 3: Crimes Act pt 3A, "intimate image abuse"
    `intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A`
    -- item 4: Crimes Act pt 4, "female genital mutilation"
    `female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4`
    -- item 5: Crimes Act pt 5, "sexual servitude"
    `sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5`
    -- item 6: Criminal Code s 309, "robbery"
    `robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309`
    -- item 7: Criminal Code s 310, "aggravated robbery"
    `aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310`
    -- div 1.2.2 items 1 to 25: property damage, arson, forcible entry, trespass, offensive weapons, offensive behaviour,
    -- burglary, threats to damage property, contravention of a family violence order, firearms, negligent, furious or
    -- menacing driving, and the rest of that division
    `an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)`
    `an offence not listed in schedule 1`

-- Dictionary: "sexual offence means an offence against a provision mentioned in schedule 1 ..., division 1.2.1 ...,
-- column 3, item 2, 4 or 5." Item 3 (intimate image abuse) is not in the list.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a sexual offence` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Dictionary: "offence against the person means an offence against a provision mentioned in schedule 1 ...,
-- division 1.2.1 ..., column 3, item 1, 6, or 7."
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence against the person` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Dictionary: "schedule 1 offence means (a) an offence against a provision mentioned in an item in schedule 1 ...,
-- division 1.2.1 ...; and (b) if the victim of an offence is a relevant person in relation to the person who carried
-- out the offence -- an offence against a provision mentioned in an item in schedule 1 ..., division 1.2.2". A relevant
-- person is a domestic or intimate partner or former partner, a relative, a child of a domestic partner or former
-- domestic partner, or a parent of a child of the person who carried out the offence (dictionary, "relevant person").
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence`
      `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a schedule 1 offence` `the offence` `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)` THEN `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`
    WHEN `an offence not listed in schedule 1` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 9 (2): "family violence offence means a schedule 1 offence for which the victim of the offence is a relevant
-- person." Wider than division 1.2.2: an assault on a partner is one too.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence`
      `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a family violence offence (s 9 (2))` `the offence` `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender` IF
        `is a schedule 1 offence` `the offence` `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`
    AND `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`

§§ `s 9 -- injury`

-- s 9 (1): injury "(a) means any of the following: (i) physical injury; (ii) mental illness; (iii) mental disorder; and
-- (b) includes (i) the aggravation, acceleration or recurrence of [any of those]; or (ii) the contraction, aggravation,
-- acceleration or recurrence of a disease; and (c) if the injury occurs in the course of, or as a result of, a sexual
-- offence or family violence offence includes (i) unplanned pregnancy; or (ii) a sense of violation; or (iii) a reduced
-- sense of self-worth; or (iv) increased fear or feelings of insecurity; or (v) reduced capacity to participate in
-- sexual activity."
DECLARE `Harm` IS ONE OF
    `a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one`
    `only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity`
    `no injury`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A `Harm`
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence`
      `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an injury (s 9)` `the harm` `the offence` `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity` THEN
            `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
        OR  `is a family violence offence (s 9 (2))` `the offence` `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 7, 10 to 17 -- act of violence, homicide, and the classes of victim`

-- s 10 (1): "homicide means an act that (a) occurs on or after the commencement of this Act; and (b) results in the death
-- of a person; and (c) is, or happens in the course of, an offence of murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing
-- death." s 11: a primary victim is one who "has been injured or dies as a direct result of an act of violence".
DECLARE `Death` IS ONE OF
    `no one died as a result of the act`
    `a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death`
    `a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence`

-- ss 13 to 15, 17: the applicant's relationship to the primary victim who died.
DECLARE `Relationship` IS ONE OF
    -- s 17 (1) (a), close family member
    `the domestic partner`
    -- s 13 (b) (ii), s 14 (b) (ii); Family Violence Act 2016, s 10
    `an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner`
    -- s 17 (1) (b), close family member; s 17 (2): not a guardian by statutory office
    `a parent, guardian or step-parent`
    -- s 17 (1) (c), close family member
    `a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian`
    -- s 15 (2), family member: (a), or (b) regarded as one under Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander tradition and custom
    `a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister`
    `another relationship, or none`

-- Is the applicant's application about their own injury, or about the death of a primary victim? A person injured in
-- the same act that killed their partner is both a primary victim and a related victim; each is its own application
-- (s 24 sets a maximum "for an application").
DECLARE `Capacity` IS ONE OF
    `an injury to the applicant`
    `the death of a person killed by the act`

-- One act of violence, from the applicant's side.
DECLARE `Victim facts` HAS
    `the day of the act`                                                IS A DATE
    `the associated offence`                                            IS AN `Associated offence`
    `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is about`                                          IS A `Capacity`
    `the applicant's harm`                                              IS A `Harm`
    `the applicant's harm is a direct result of the act`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death`                                                         IS A `Death`
    `the applicant's relationship to the person who died`               IS A `Relationship`
    -- dictionary, "dependant": wholly or partly dependent for economic support at the death, or would have been but for
    -- the incapacity the act caused, or a child born after the death who would have been
    `the applicant was a dependant of the person who died`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant was present at the homicide or is a witness in its investigation or a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is a perpetrator of the homicide`                    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Victim class` IS ONE OF
    `a primary victim (s 11)`
    `a class A related victim (s 13)`
    `a class B related victim (s 14)`
    `a class C related victim (s 15)`
    `a homicide witness (s 16)`
    `not a victim in that capacity (ss 11 to 16)`
    `not a victim: the conduct is not an act of violence (s 7)`
    `not covered: the act happened before 1 July 2016 (s 98)`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person died` `the facts` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the death`
    WHEN `no one died as a result of the act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death was a homicide (s 10)` `the facts` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the death`
    WHEN `a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is injured (s 9)` `the facts` IF
    `is an injury (s 9)` (`the facts`'s `the applicant's harm`) (`the facts`'s `the associated offence`) (`the facts`'s `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`)

-- s 7 (1): "act of violence means conduct that (a) results in a person's injury or death; and (b) is, or happens in the
-- course of, an offence (the associated offence) that is (i) a schedule 1 offence; or (ii) an offence prescribed by
-- regulation; and (c) occurs on or after the commencement of this Act." s 7 (2): it does not matter whether the person
-- responsible has been identified, lacks legal capacity, or has been charged or convicted.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an act of violence (s 7)` `the facts` IF
        (   `the applicant is injured (s 9)` `the facts`
         OR `a person died` `the facts`)
    AND `is a schedule 1 offence` (`the facts`'s `the associated offence`) (`the facts`'s `the victim is a relevant person in relation to the offender`)
    AND `is on or before` `the commencement of the Act` (`the facts`'s `the day of the act`)

-- s 17 (1): close family member: the domestic partner; a parent, guardian or step-parent; a child or stepchild, or a
-- child of whom the primary victim is the guardian.
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a close family member or intimate partner (ss 13, 14, 17)` `the relationship` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `the domestic partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a parent, guardian or step-parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a family member (s 15 (2))` `the relationship` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 13: class A, "at the time a primary victim dies (a) is a dependant of the primary victim; and (b) is 1 of the
-- following: (i) a close family member of the primary victim; (ii) an intimate partner of the primary victim."
-- s 14: class B, the same but "(a) is financially independent of the primary victim". s 15: class C, "(a) is
-- financially independent of the primary victim; and (b) is a family member of the primary victim".
-- Dictionary: "financially independent ... means a person who is not dependant on the primary victim".
-- A dependent brother or sister fits none of the three (NOTES.md finding).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A `Victim class`
`the related victim class of` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `a person died` `the facts`
    THEN IF `is a close family member or intimate partner (ss 13, 14, 17)` (`the facts`'s `the applicant's relationship to the person who died`)
         THEN IF `the facts`'s `the applicant was a dependant of the person who died`
              THEN `a class A related victim (s 13)`
              ELSE `a class B related victim (s 14)`
         ELSE IF     `is a family member (s 15 (2))` (`the facts`'s `the applicant's relationship to the person who died`)
                 AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the applicant was a dependant of the person who died`))
              THEN `a class C related victim (s 15)`
              ELSE `not a victim in that capacity (ss 11 to 16)`
    ELSE `not a victim in that capacity (ss 11 to 16)`

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a related victim class` `the class` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a class A related victim (s 13)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class B related victim (s 14)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class C related victim (s 15)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 16: "homicide witness, in relation to a homicide, means a person, other than a primary victim, a related victim or a
-- perpetrator of the homicide, who has been injured as a result of (a) being present when the homicide occurs; or
-- (b) being a witness in a criminal investigation or a proceeding related to the homicide."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a homicide witness (s 16)` `the facts` IF
        `the death was a homicide (s 10)` `the facts`
    AND `the applicant is injured (s 9)` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `the applicant was present at the homicide or is a witness in its investigation or a proceeding`
    AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the applicant is a perpetrator of the homicide`))
    AND (NOT (`is a related victim class` (`the related victim class of` `the facts`)))

-- s 11: "primary victim means a person who has been injured or dies as a direct result of an act of violence done by
-- another person." ss 12 to 16 as above.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A `Victim class`
`the victim class of` `the facts` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL (`the facts`'s `the day of the act`) LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the commencement of the Act`
    THEN `not covered: the act happened before 1 July 2016 (s 98)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the conduct is an act of violence (s 7)` `the facts`)
         THEN `not a victim: the conduct is not an act of violence (s 7)`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the application is about`
              WHEN `an injury to the applicant` THEN
                  IF      `the applicant is injured (s 9)` `the facts`
                      AND `the facts`'s `the applicant's harm is a direct result of the act`
                  THEN `a primary victim (s 11)`
                  ELSE IF `is a homicide witness (s 16)` `the facts`
                       THEN `a homicide witness (s 16)`
                       ELSE `not a victim in that capacity (ss 11 to 16)`
              WHEN `the death of a person killed by the act` THEN `the related victim class of` `the facts`

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a victim` `the class` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a primary victim (s 11)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class A related victim (s 13)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class B related victim (s 14)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class C related victim (s 15)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a homicide witness (s 16)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the act before the Act` `the class` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `not covered: the act happened before 1 July 2016 (s 98)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `Part 3 -- financial assistance`

§§ `Division 3.1 -- who may apply for which payment (ss 18 to 23)`

DECLARE `Payment kind` IS ONE OF
    `an immediate need payment (s 26)`
    `an economic loss payment (s 27)`
    `a recognition payment (ss 28 to 30)`

-- s 19 primary victim, s 20 class A, s 21 class B: "(a) an immediate need payment; (b) an economic loss payment;
-- (c) a recognition payment." s 22 class C, s 23 homicide witness: "(a) an immediate need payment; (b) an economic loss
-- payment." s 18: "Financial assistance may only be given to a person who is eligible to apply".
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Payment kind`
`the payments the class may apply for (ss 19 to 23)` `the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a primary victim (s 11)` THEN LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`, `a recognition payment (ss 28 to 30)`
    WHEN `a class A related victim (s 13)` THEN LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`, `a recognition payment (ss 28 to 30)`
    WHEN `a class B related victim (s 14)` THEN LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`, `a recognition payment (ss 28 to 30)`
    WHEN `a class C related victim (s 15)` THEN LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`
    WHEN `a homicide witness (s 16)` THEN LIST `an immediate need payment (s 26)`, `an economic loss payment (s 27)`
    OTHERWISE EMPTY

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for a recognition payment` `the class` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a primary victim (s 11)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class A related victim (s 13)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class B related victim (s 14)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Eligibility answer` IS ONE OF
    `may apply for` HAS `the payments` IS A LIST OF `Payment kind`
    `may not apply: not a victim under the Act (ss 7, 11 to 18)`
    `eligibility not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`the eligibility answer for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `is victim` THEN `may apply for` (`the payments the class may apply for (ss 19 to 23)` `the class`)
    ELSE IF `is the act before the Act` `the class`
         THEN `eligibility not covered` `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
         ELSE `may not apply: not a victim under the Act (ss 7, 11 to 18)`
    WHERE
        `the class` MEANS `the victim class of` `the facts`
        `is victim` MEANS `is a victim` `the class`

§§ `Answers that carry an amount`

DECLARE `Payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `the most that can be paid, in dollars` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `none: not eligible to apply for this payment (ss 18 to 23)`
    `none: not available for this loss or need to this applicant (reg ss 6 and 7, column 3)`
    `none: the act of violence did not occur in the course of an offence in table 8 (reg s 8)`
    `none: financial assistance must not be given, as a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45)`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- For a person who is not a victim, the answer is `none`, or `not covered` for an act before 1 July 2016.
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
      `the answer for a victim` IS A `Payment answer`
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`for a victim only` `the class` `the answer for a victim` MEANS
    IF `is a victim` `the class`
    THEN `the answer for a victim`
    ELSE IF `is the act before the Act` `the class`
         THEN `not covered` `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
         ELSE `none: not eligible to apply for this payment (ss 18 to 23)`

§§ `Division 3.2 -- the maximum total (s 24, reg s 5)`

-- s 24: "The maximum total amount of financial assistance that may be given to a person for an application for
-- financial assistance is the amount prescribed by regulation." Reg s 5 (1): "(a) for a primary victim -- $67 959;
-- (b) for a class A related victim -- $40 773; (c) for a class B related victim -- $27 183; (d) for a class C related
-- victim -- $13 590; (e) for a homicide witness -- $13 590." (2): "However, if an application for financial assistance
-- relates only to an act of violence that occurs in the course of an offence mentioned in the Act, schedule 1,
-- division 1.2.2 (Family violence offences), the amount prescribed is $13 590."
`the reg s 5 (2) amount` MEANS 13590

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reg s 5 (1) amount for` `the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a primary victim (s 11)` THEN 67959
    WHEN `a class A related victim (s 13)` THEN 40773
    WHEN `a class B related victim (s 14)` THEN 27183
    WHEN `a class C related victim (s 15)` THEN 13590
    WHEN `a homicide witness (s 16)` THEN 13590
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application relates only to a division 1.2.2 offence` `the facts` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the associated offence`
    WHEN `an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The maximum, in dollars, for a victim (0 for anyone else; callers check the class first).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 24 maximum in dollars for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the application relates only to a division 1.2.2 offence` `the facts`
    THEN `the reg s 5 (2) amount`
    ELSE `the reg s 5 (1) amount for` (`the victim class of` `the facts`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the s 24 maximum total for` `the facts` MEANS
    `for a victim only` (`the victim class of` `the facts`) (`the most that can be paid, in dollars` (`the s 24 maximum in dollars for` `the facts`))

§§ `Division 3.3 -- immediate need payment (s 26, reg s 6, table 6)`

-- s 26 (1): "A financial payment (an immediate need payment) may be made to a person for reasonable expenses incurred,
-- or expected to be incurred, for an immediate need that is related to an act of violence." (2): an expense is reasonable
-- if, when the application is made, paying it is likely to promote recovery, prevent further harm or limit further
-- threats to safety: a judgment for the commissioner, so every amount here is the most that CAN be paid.
-- Table 6: item 1 "cleaning scene of homicide" $5 000; item 2 "measures for personal security of a victim" $4 000;
-- item 3 "relocation for personal security of a victim" $4 000; item 4 "emergency medical costs and related services
-- that would contribute to victim's recovery", "only available if applicant does not have financial ability to pay for
-- treatment or service" and "not available for homicide witness", $10 000. (The deposited text runs the two item 4
-- conditions together; they are read as two.) Reg s 6 (4): "The maximum aggregate amount of all immediate need payments
-- that may be made for a single act of violence is $10 000" -- for the act, whoever applies.
DECLARE `Immediate need claim` HAS
    `cleaning the scene of a homicide`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `measures for the personal security of a victim`                     IS A NUMBER
    `relocation for the personal security of a victim`                   IS A NUMBER
    `emergency medical costs and related services`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the applicant does not have the financial ability to pay for the treatment or service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediate need payments already made to anyone for the same act of violence` IS A NUMBER

`the table 6 item 1 maximum` MEANS 5000
`the table 6 item 2 maximum` MEANS 4000
`the table 6 item 3 maximum` MEANS 4000
`the table 6 item 4 maximum` MEANS 10000
`the reg s 6 (4) aggregate for a single act of violence` MEANS 10000

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the claim` IS AN `Immediate need claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the immediate need dollars for` `the facts` `the claim` MEANS
    min (`what is left for the act`) (`item 1` PLUS `item 2` PLUS `item 3` PLUS `item 4`)
    WHERE
        -- item 1 is the need to clean the scene of a homicide; without a homicide there is no such need
        `item 1` MEANS
            IF `the death was a homicide (s 10)` `the facts`
            THEN min (`the claim`'s `cleaning the scene of a homicide`) `the table 6 item 1 maximum`
            ELSE 0
        `item 2` MEANS min (`the claim`'s `measures for the personal security of a victim`) `the table 6 item 2 maximum`
        `item 3` MEANS min (`the claim`'s `relocation for the personal security of a victim`) `the table 6 item 3 maximum`
        `item 4` MEANS
            IF      `the claim`'s `the applicant does not have the financial ability to pay for the treatment or service`
                AND (NOT (`the victim class of` `the facts` EQUALS `a homicide witness (s 16)`))
            THEN min (`the claim`'s `emergency medical costs and related services`) `the table 6 item 4 maximum`
            ELSE 0
        `what is left for the act` MEANS
            max 0 (`the reg s 6 (4) aggregate for a single act of violence` MINUS `the claim`'s `immediate need payments already made to anyone for the same act of violence`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the claim` IS AN `Immediate need claim`
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the immediate need payment answer for` `the facts` `the claim` MEANS
    `for a victim only` (`the victim class of` `the facts`) (`the most that can be paid, in dollars` (`the immediate need dollars for` `the facts` `the claim`))

§§ `Division 3.3 -- economic loss payment (s 27, reg s 7, table 7)`

-- s 27 (1): "A financial payment (an economic loss payment) may be made to a person for economic loss sustained as a
-- result of an act of violence." Table 7, column 2 (loss), column 3 (condition), column 4 (maximum):
--   1 "expenses for counselling or other psychological support": "only available if the person applying ... was not able
--     to access appropriate counselling or other psychological support under the victims services scheme"
--   2 "expenses, other than legal costs, incurred in making the application"
--   3 "medical and dental expenses": "not available for a homicide witness"
--   4 "travel expenses": "not available for a homicide witness"
--   5 "justice related expenses": "not available for a homicide witness"; $5 000
--   6 "loss of actual earnings (including loss of earnings incurred by the parent or carer of a primary victim ...)":
--     "not available for a homicide witness"; $30 000
--   7 "reasonable expenses incurred by the parent or carer of a primary victim as a result of an act of violence": "an
--     amount given to a parent or carer ... is counted as part of the maximum amount prescribed for the primary victim
--     under s 5" and "not available for a homicide witness" (run together in the deposited text; read as two)
--   8 "other expenses in exceptional circumstances": "not available for a homicide witness"
--   9 "loss of or damage to personal items": "only available for a primary victim"; $1 500
-- No item 1 to 4, 7 or 8 maximum, and no s 27 (2) (d) aggregate: only s 24 limits them.
DECLARE `Economic loss kind` IS ONE OF
    `expenses for counselling or other psychological support`
    `expenses, other than legal costs, of making the application`
    `medical and dental expenses`
    `travel expenses`
    `justice related expenses`
    `loss of actual earnings`
    `reasonable expenses of the parent or carer of a primary victim`
    `other expenses in exceptional circumstances`
    `loss of or damage to personal items`

-- The table 7 column 4 maximum, if any.
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Economic loss kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the table 7 maximum for` `the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `justice related expenses` THEN JUST 5000
    WHEN `loss of actual earnings` THEN JUST 30000
    WHEN `loss of or damage to personal items` THEN JUST 1500
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The table 7 column 3 condition.
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Economic loss kind`
      `the class` IS A `Victim class`
      `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the table 7 condition is met for` `the kind` `the class` `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `expenses for counselling or other psychological support` THEN `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme`
    WHEN `expenses, other than legal costs, of making the application` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `loss of or damage to personal items` THEN `the class` EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
    OTHERWISE NOT (`the class` EQUALS `a homicide witness (s 16)`)

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Economic loss kind`
      `the class` IS A `Victim class`
      `the amount claimed` IS A NUMBER
      `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the economic loss dollars for` `the kind` `the class` `the amount claimed` `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` MEANS
    IF `the table 7 condition is met for` `the kind` `the class` `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme`
    THEN CONSIDER `the table 7 maximum for` `the kind`
         WHEN JUST `the cap` THEN min `the amount claimed` `the cap`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the amount claimed`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the kind` IS AN `Economic loss kind`
      `the amount claimed` IS A NUMBER
      `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the economic loss payment answer for` `the facts` `the kind` `the amount claimed` `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` MEANS
    `for a victim only` `the class`
        (IF `the table 7 condition is met for` `the kind` `the class` `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme`
         THEN `the most that can be paid, in dollars` (`the economic loss dollars for` `the kind` `the class` `the amount claimed` `appropriate counselling was not available under the victims services scheme`)
         ELSE `none: not available for this loss or need to this applicant (reg ss 6 and 7, column 3)`)
    WHERE
        `the class` MEANS `the victim class of` `the facts`

-- Every table 7 loss in one application.
DECLARE `Economic loss claim` HAS
    `counselling or other psychological support`                        IS A NUMBER
    `expenses of making the application, other than legal costs`       IS A NUMBER
    `medical and dental`                                                IS A NUMBER
    `travel`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `justice related`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `actual earnings lost`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the parent's or carer's reasonable expenses`                       IS A NUMBER
    `other expenses in exceptional circumstances claimed`               IS A NUMBER
    `personal items lost or damaged`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `counselling was not available under the victims services scheme`  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the claim` IS AN `Economic loss claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the economic loss dollars for the claim` `the facts` `the claim` MEANS
    sum (LIST
        `for` `expenses for counselling or other psychological support` (`the claim`'s `counselling or other psychological support`),
        `for` `expenses, other than legal costs, of making the application` (`the claim`'s `expenses of making the application, other than legal costs`),
        `for` `medical and dental expenses` (`the claim`'s `medical and dental`),
        `for` `travel expenses` (`the claim`'s `travel`),
        `for` `justice related expenses` (`the claim`'s `justice related`),
        `for` `loss of actual earnings` (`the claim`'s `actual earnings lost`),
        `for` `reasonable expenses of the parent or carer of a primary victim` (`the claim`'s `the parent's or carer's reasonable expenses`),
        `for` `other expenses in exceptional circumstances` (`the claim`'s `other expenses in exceptional circumstances claimed`),
        `for` `loss of or damage to personal items` (`the claim`'s `personal items lost or damaged`))
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Economic loss kind`
              `the amount` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `for` `the kind` `the amount` MEANS
            `the economic loss dollars for` `the kind` (`the victim class of` `the facts`) `the amount` (`the claim`'s `counselling was not available under the victims services scheme`)

§§ `Division 3.3 -- recognition payments (ss 28 to 30, reg ss 8 to 10, table 8)`

-- s 28 (1): a recognition payment "may be made to a primary victim for trauma experienced by the primary victim as a
-- result of an act of violence". Reg s 8 (1): the act "must occur" in the course of an offence in table 8, column 2;
-- (2): the amount is in column 3.
DECLARE `Table 8 offence` IS ONE OF
    -- item 1, $20 386
    `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more`
    -- item 2, $20 386
    `an attempt or conspiracy to commit homicide`
    -- item 3, $10 873
    `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years`
    -- item 4, $10 873
    `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm`
    -- item 5, $10 873
    `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more`
    -- item 6, $2 716
    `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years`
    -- item 7, $2 716
    `an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm`
    -- item 8, $2 716
    `robbery in company or with an offensive weapon`
    -- item 9, $2 716
    `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years`
    -- item 10, $2 716
    `an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm`
    -- item 11, $2 716
    `an offence involving deprivation of liberty, including kidnapping and forcible confinement`
    -- item 12, $1 357
    `an offence against the person not resulting in actual bodily harm`
    -- item 13, $1 357
    `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years`
    -- item 14, $1 357
    `an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm`
    `none of the offences in table 8`

-- Reg s 8 (3): "If the Crimes Act 1900, section 66 (1) (b), applies to an offence mentioned in table 8, column 2,
-- item 3, the offence is taken to be an offence mentioned in table 8, column 2, item 6."
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Table 8 offence`
      `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the table 8 amount for` `the offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more` THEN 20386
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit homicide` THEN 20386
    WHEN `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years` THEN
        IF `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` THEN 2716 ELSE 10873
    WHEN `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` THEN 10873
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more` THEN 10873
    WHEN `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years` THEN 2716
    WHEN `an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm` THEN 2716
    WHEN `robbery in company or with an offensive weapon` THEN 2716
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years` THEN 2716
    WHEN `an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` THEN 2716
    WHEN `an offence involving deprivation of liberty, including kidnapping and forcible confinement` THEN 2716
    WHEN `an offence against the person not resulting in actual bodily harm` THEN 1357
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years` THEN 1357
    WHEN `an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm` THEN 1357
    OTHERWISE 0

-- Table 8's column 2 uses the dictionary's "sexual offence" (sch 1 div 1.2.1 items 2, 4, 5) and "offence against the
-- person" (items 1, 6, 7). An item in those terms fits only an act in the course of such an offence. Items 2, 8 and 11
-- are not framed in a defined term and fit any schedule 1 offence. So intimate image abuse (item 3 of div 1.2.1) and
-- the division 1.2.2 offences reach only items 2, 8 and 11 (NOTES.md finding).
GIVEN `the table 8 offence` IS A `Table 8 offence`
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the table 8 item fits the associated offence` `the table 8 offence` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the table 8 offence`
    WHEN `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more` THEN `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
    WHEN `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years` THEN `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more` THEN `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
    WHEN `a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years` THEN `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years` THEN `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
    WHEN `an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years` THEN `is a sexual offence` `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` THEN `is an offence against the person` `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm` THEN `is an offence against the person` `the offence`
    WHEN `an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm` THEN `is an offence against the person` `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence against the person not resulting in actual bodily harm` THEN `is an offence against the person` `the offence`
    WHEN `an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm` THEN `is an offence against the person` `the offence`
    WHEN `none of the offences in table 8` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Reg s 9 (Act s 29 (2)): class A, "$27 183". Reg s 10 (Act s 30 (2)): class B, "$13 590".
`the reg s 9 class A recognition payment` MEANS 27183
`the reg s 10 class B recognition payment` MEANS 13590

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the table 8 offence` IS A `Table 8 offence`
      `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the recognition payment answer for` `the facts` `the table 8 offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` MEANS
    `for a victim only` `the class`
        (CONSIDER `the class`
         WHEN `a primary victim (s 11)` THEN
             IF `the table 8 item fits the associated offence` `the table 8 offence` (`the facts`'s `the associated offence`)
             THEN `the most that can be paid, in dollars` (`the table 8 amount for` `the table 8 offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies`)
             ELSE `none: the act of violence did not occur in the course of an offence in table 8 (reg s 8)`
         WHEN `a class A related victim (s 13)` THEN `the most that can be paid, in dollars` `the reg s 9 class A recognition payment`
         WHEN `a class B related victim (s 14)` THEN `the most that can be paid, in dollars` `the reg s 10 class B recognition payment`
         OTHERWISE `none: not eligible to apply for this payment (ss 18 to 23)`)
    WHERE
        `the class` MEANS `the victim class of` `the facts`

-- The recognition payment in dollars, 0 where none.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the table 8 offence` IS A `Table 8 offence`
      `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recognition dollars for` `the facts` `the table 8 offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the recognition payment answer for` `the facts` `the table 8 offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies`
    WHEN `the most that can be paid, in dollars` `the dollars` THEN `the dollars`
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `Division 3.6 -- when assistance must not be given, and reductions (ss 45 to 47)`

-- s 45 (1): a disqualifying circumstance is "(a) the applicant is not eligible for the assistance; (b) the applicant
-- conspired with the person responsible for the act of violence ...; (c) the applicant was involved in a serious crime
-- when the act of violence ... occurred and the serious crime was the main reason that the act of violence occurred;
-- (d) the applicant is claiming financial assistance as a related victim for the act of violence ... that was related to
-- a serious crime carried out by the primary victim; (e) the applicant has unreasonably failed to give assistance to the
-- police in relation to the act of violence". (4): "If the commissioner decides that a disqualifying circumstance
-- applies ... the commissioner must not give financial assistance". Each of (b) to (e) is the commissioner's finding,
-- made after the s 45 (2) notice and the applicant's reply: here they are facts.
DECLARE `Conduct findings` HAS
    `the applicant conspired with the person responsible for the act`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant was involved in a serious crime that was the main reason the act occurred`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police`                             IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the findings` IS A `Conduct findings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e))` `the facts` `the findings` IF
        `the findings`'s `the applicant conspired with the person responsible for the act`
    OR  `the findings`'s `the applicant was involved in a serious crime that was the main reason the act occurred`
    OR  (    `is a related victim class` (`the victim class of` `the facts`)
         AND `the findings`'s `the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim`)
    OR  `the findings`'s `the applicant unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police`

DECLARE `Refusal answer` IS ONE OF
    `no disqualifying circumstance applies on these findings (s 45)`
    `assistance must not be given: the applicant is not eligible for it (s 45 (1) (a))`
    `assistance must not be given: a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e), (4))`
    `refusal not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the findings` IS A `Conduct findings`
GIVETH A `Refusal answer`
`the s 45 answer for` `the facts` `the findings` MEANS
    IF `is the act before the Act` (`the victim class of` `the facts`)
    THEN `refusal not covered` `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
    ELSE IF NOT (`is a victim` (`the victim class of` `the facts`))
         THEN `assistance must not be given: the applicant is not eligible for it (s 45 (1) (a))`
         ELSE IF `a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e))` `the facts` `the findings`
              THEN `assistance must not be given: a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e), (4))`
              ELSE `no disqualifying circumstance applies on these findings (s 45)`

-- s 47 (1), (2): the commissioner "must reduce the amount of financial assistance to the applicant by an amount
-- (a) ... equal to the associated payment [covering the same harm or loss]; or (b) [for an unpaid part 5 or part 6
-- repayment] ... equal to the outstanding repayment amount; or (c) [for contributory conduct] ... that the commissioner
-- is satisfied is appropriate". The contributory-conduct amount is the commissioner's: an input.
DECLARE `Reductions` HAS
    `associated payments covering the same harm or loss`                 IS A NUMBER
    `outstanding repayment amounts under part 5 or part 6`               IS A NUMBER
    `the reduction for contributory conduct that the commissioner decides` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the reductions` IS A `Reductions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 47 reduction` `the reductions` MEANS
        `the reductions`'s `associated payments covering the same harm or loss`
    PLUS `the reductions`'s `outstanding repayment amounts under part 5 or part 6`
    PLUS `the reductions`'s `the reduction for contributory conduct that the commissioner decides`

-- All claims in one application. READING: the s 47 reduction comes off the amount after the s 24 maximum (s 46 (2) (d)
-- reduces "the amount" decided; s 24 is the most that "may be given"). The Act does not say which comes first.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the immediate need claim` IS AN `Immediate need claim`
      `the economic loss claim` IS AN `Economic loss claim`
      `claims a recognition payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the table 8 offence` IS A `Table 8 offence`
      `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the findings` IS A `Conduct findings`
      `the reductions` IS A `Reductions`
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the total financial assistance answer for` `the facts` `the immediate need claim` `the economic loss claim` `claims a recognition payment` `the table 8 offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies` `the findings` `the reductions` MEANS
    `for a victim only` (`the victim class of` `the facts`)
        (IF `a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45 (1) (b) to (e))` `the facts` `the findings`
         THEN `none: financial assistance must not be given, as a disqualifying circumstance applies (s 45)`
         ELSE `the most that can be paid, in dollars` (max 0 (`within the maximum` MINUS `the s 47 reduction` `the reductions`)))
    WHERE
        `recognition` MEANS
            IF `claims a recognition payment`
            THEN `the recognition dollars for` `the facts` `the table 8 offence` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies`
            ELSE 0
        `claimed` MEANS
                `the immediate need dollars for` `the facts` `the immediate need claim`
            PLUS `the economic loss dollars for the claim` `the facts` `the economic loss claim`
            PLUS `recognition`
        `within the maximum` MEANS min `claimed` (`the s 24 maximum in dollars for` `the facts`)

§§ `Division 3.4 -- the application, its evidence and its time (ss 31, 32)`

-- s 31 (4): "An applicant is a special reporting class victim if, in relation to an act of violence that is the subject
-- of an application, the applicant is a primary victim (a) of a sexual offence; or (b) of an offence in which the person
-- responsible for the act of violence against the primary victim was in a position of power, trust or authority in
-- relation to the primary victim; or (c) who has impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity; or (d) who
-- was under 18 years old when the act of violence occurred; or (e) who did not report the act of violence to police
-- because of threats made, or intimidation by, another person."
DECLARE `Special reporting facts` HAS
    `the person responsible was in a position of power, trust or authority over the primary victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant has impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant's date of birth`                                                                  IS A DATE
    `the applicant did not report to police because of threats or intimidation`                      IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th birthday of a person born on` `the date of birth` MEANS
    18 `years after` `the date of birth`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was under 18 on` `the day` `for a person born on` `the date of birth` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the 18th birthday of a person born on` `the date of birth`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the special facts` IS A `Special reporting facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a special reporting class victim (s 31 (4))` `the facts` `the special facts` IF
        `the victim class of` `the facts` EQUALS `a primary victim (s 11)`
    AND (   `is a sexual offence` (`the facts`'s `the associated offence`)
         OR `the special facts`'s `the person responsible was in a position of power, trust or authority over the primary victim`
         OR `the special facts`'s `the applicant has impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity`
         OR `was under 18 on` (`the facts`'s `the day of the act`) `for a person born on` (`the special facts`'s `the applicant's date of birth`)
         OR `the special facts`'s `the applicant did not report to police because of threats or intimidation`)

-- s 31 (2): the application must "(a) be in writing; and (b) include a contact address for the applicant; and
-- (c) indicate the financial assistance payment that the applicant wishes to claim; and (d) be accompanied by evidence
-- that (i) the act of violence ... has been reported to a police officer; or (ii) if the applicant is a special reporting
-- class victim and the application does not include a claim for a recognition payment -- the act of violence ... has
-- been reported in accordance with subsection (5)." (3): "the application need not comply with the requirement under
-- subsection (2) (d) (i) if the act of violence was carried out by a person who was under the age of criminal
-- responsibility". READING: (2) (d) is then met without evidence of any report. (5) (a): for an immediate need payment
-- only, a report "to at least 2 of the following: (i) a government agency; (ii) a doctor or a psychologist or a
-- counsellor or a social worker; (iii) an appropriately qualified non-government agency"; (b): for an economic loss
-- payment, with or without an immediate need payment, a report "to both of the following: (i) a government agency;
-- (ii) a doctor or a psychologist or a counsellor or a social worker". (6): an appropriately qualified non-government
-- agency is one specified in the commissioner's guidelines (not deposited): the applicant's answer is taken.
DECLARE `Application facts` HAS
    `is in writing`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes a contact address`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `indicates the payments claimed`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims an immediate need payment`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims an economic loss payment`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims a recognition payment in the application`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was reported to a police officer`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was reported to a government agency`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was reported to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was reported to an appropriately qualified non-government agency`   IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Evidence answer` IS ONE OF
    `no evidence of a report is needed: the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility (s 31 (3))`
    `evidence that the act was reported to a police officer (s 31 (2) (d) (i))`
    `evidence of a police report, or of reports to at least 2 of: a government agency; a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker; an appropriately qualified non-government agency (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (a))`
    `evidence of a police report, or of reports to both a government agency and a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (b))`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the special facts` IS A `Special reporting facts`
      `the application` IS AN `Application facts`
GIVETH AN `Evidence answer`
`the s 31 evidence needed for` `the facts` `the special facts` `the application` MEANS
    IF `the application`'s `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility`
    THEN `no evidence of a report is needed: the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility (s 31 (3))`
    ELSE IF     `is a special reporting class victim (s 31 (4))` `the facts` `the special facts`
            AND (NOT (`the application`'s `claims a recognition payment in the application`))
         THEN IF `the application`'s `claims an economic loss payment`
              THEN `evidence of a police report, or of reports to both a government agency and a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (b))`
              ELSE `evidence of a police report, or of reports to at least 2 of: a government agency; a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker; an appropriately qualified non-government agency (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (a))`
         ELSE `evidence that the act was reported to a police officer (s 31 (2) (d) (i))`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the special facts` IS A `Special reporting facts`
      `the application` IS AN `Application facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the evidence meets s 31 (2) (d)` `the facts` `the special facts` `the application` IF
    CONSIDER `the s 31 evidence needed for` `the facts` `the special facts` `the application`
    WHEN `no evidence of a report is needed: the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility (s 31 (3))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `evidence that the act was reported to a police officer (s 31 (2) (d) (i))` THEN `police`
    WHEN `evidence of a police report, or of reports to at least 2 of: a government agency; a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker; an appropriately qualified non-government agency (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (a))` THEN
            `police`
        OR  (`count` `agency` PLUS `count` `practitioner` PLUS `count` `non-government agency`) AT LEAST 2
    WHEN `evidence of a police report, or of reports to both a government agency and a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker (s 31 (2) (d), (5) (b))` THEN
            `police`
        OR  (`agency` AND `practitioner`)
    WHERE
        `police` MEANS `the application`'s `the act was reported to a police officer`
        `agency` MEANS `the application`'s `the act was reported to a government agency`
        `practitioner` MEANS `the application`'s `the act was reported to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker`
        `non-government agency` MEANS `the application`'s `the act was reported to an appropriately qualified non-government agency`
        GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `count` `b` MEANS IF `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Victim facts`
      `the special facts` IS A `Special reporting facts`
      `the application` IS AN `Application facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application complies with s 31 (2)` `the facts` `the special facts` `the application` IF
        `the application`'s `is in writing`
    AND `the application`'s `includes a contact address`
    AND `the application`'s `indicates the payments claimed`
    AND `the evidence meets s 31 (2) (d)` `the facts` `the special facts` `the application`

-- s 32 (1): "An application under section 31 must be made within 3 years of the last occurring of the following: (a) the
-- day of the act of violence that is the subject of the application; (b) if there are 2 or more relevant acts of
-- violence -- the day of the most recent act of violence; (c) for an application by an individual who was under 18 years
-- old on the day mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) -- the day the individual turns 18." The 18th birthday is later than
-- (a) or (b) exactly when the person was under 18 on that day, so the latest of the three days is the start.
-- READING: "within 3 years of" a day ends on its third anniversary.
`the years to apply for financial assistance (s 32 (1))` MEANS 3

GIVEN `the day of the most recent act` IS A DATE
      `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for financial assistance (s 32 (1))` `the day of the most recent act` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `the years to apply for financial assistance (s 32 (1))` `years after`
        (`the later of` `the day of the most recent act` `and` (`the 18th birthday of a person born on` `the date of birth`))

-- s 32 (2): "The commissioner may extend the time ... if the commissioner believes on reasonable grounds that an
-- extension is in the interests of fairness having regard to" the age of the person at the act, impaired capacity, a
-- person responsible in a position of power, trust or authority, the physical and psychological effect of the act,
-- whether the extension will prevent a fair consideration, and any other relevant matter. A judgment: answered
-- conditionally.
DECLARE `Time answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: made on or before the last day (s 32 (1))`
    `late: the commissioner may extend the time if satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is in the interests of fairness, having regard to the person's age at the act, impaired capacity, a person responsible in a position of power, trust or authority, the effect of the act, and whether a fair consideration is still possible (s 32 (2))`

GIVEN `the day of the most recent act` IS A DATE
      `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time answer`
`the s 32 answer for` `the day of the most recent act` `the date of birth` `the day of the application` MEANS
    IF `is on or before` `the day of the application` (`the last day to apply for financial assistance (s 32 (1))` `the day of the most recent act` `the date of birth`)
    THEN `in time: made on or before the last day (s 32 (1))`
    ELSE `late: the commissioner may extend the time if satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is in the interests of fairness, having regard to the person's age at the act, impaired capacity, a person responsible in a position of power, trust or authority, the effect of the act, and whether a fair consideration is still possible (s 32 (2))`

-- s 45 (2) (b): the commissioner's notice asks the applicant "to tell the commissioner, in writing, within 14 days after
-- the notice is received, if there is a reason why the disqualifying circumstance does not apply."
`the days to answer a notice of a disqualifying circumstance (s 45 (2) (b))` MEANS 14

§ `Part 4 -- funeral expense payment (ss 51 to 54, s 60, reg s 11)`

-- s 51: "A person is eligible to apply to the commissioner for a funeral expense payment if the person has paid, or is
-- required to pay, the costs of a funeral for a primary victim who died as a result of homicide." s 53: the maximum is
-- "the lesser of (a) the reasonable costs of a funeral ...; (b) an amount prescribed by regulation as the maximum funeral
-- expense payment." Reg s 11: "$8 000". s 54: "within 3 years after the day of the death of the primary victim." There
-- is no power to extend it (contrast s 32 (2)). s 60 (2): divisions 3.5 and 3.6 apply, so s 45 (no payment where a
-- disqualifying circumstance applies) and s 47 (a) (reduction by an associated payment for the same loss) apply too.
`the reg s 11 maximum funeral expense payment` MEANS 8000
`the years to apply for a funeral expense payment (s 54)` MEANS 3

DECLARE `Funeral facts` HAS
    `the day of the fatal act`                                          IS A DATE
    `the fatal offence`                                                 IS AN `Associated offence`
    `the person who died was a relevant person in relation to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the way the person died`                                           IS A `Death`
    `the applicant has paid or is required to pay the funeral costs`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reasonable costs of the funeral`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the day of the death`                                              IS A DATE
    `the day of the funeral application`                                IS A DATE
    `the conduct findings for the funeral application`                  IS A `Conduct findings`
    `associated payments covering the funeral costs`                    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for a funeral expense payment (s 54)` `the day of the death` MEANS
    `the years to apply for a funeral expense payment (s 54)` `years after` `the day of the death`

-- The person who died is "a primary victim who died as a result of homicide": a death as a direct result of an act of
-- violence (a schedule 1 offence on or after 1 July 2016) that is murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death.
GIVEN `the funeral facts` IS A `Funeral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person who died was a primary victim of a homicide` `the funeral facts` IF
        `the way the person died` EQUALS `a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death`
    AND `is a schedule 1 offence` (`the funeral facts`'s `the fatal offence`) (`the funeral facts`'s `the person who died was a relevant person in relation to the offender`)
    WHERE
        `the way the person died` MEANS `the funeral facts`'s `the way the person died`

-- s 60 (2) applies division 3.6 "as if a reference to an application for financial assistance ... was a reference to a
-- funeral expense payment application". READING: s 45 (1) (b), (c) and (e) then apply to the funeral applicant; (d)
-- speaks of "claiming financial assistance as a related victim", which a funeral applicant is not doing, so it does not.
GIVEN `the findings` IS A `Conduct findings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a disqualifying circumstance applies to a funeral application (ss 45, 60)` `the findings` IF
        `the findings`'s `the applicant conspired with the person responsible for the act`
    OR  `the findings`'s `the applicant was involved in a serious crime that was the main reason the act occurred`
    OR  `the findings`'s `the applicant unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police`

DECLARE `Funeral answer` IS ONE OF
    `a funeral expense payment of at most, in dollars` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no funeral expense payment: not eligible, as the applicant has not paid and is not required to pay the funeral costs of a primary victim who died as a result of homicide (s 51)`
    `no funeral expense payment: the application is more than 3 years after the death, and the Act gives no power to extend that time (s 54)`
    `no funeral expense payment: a disqualifying circumstance applies (ss 45 and 60)`
    `funeral not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the funeral facts` IS A `Funeral facts`
GIVETH A `Funeral answer`
`the funeral expense answer for` `the funeral facts` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL (`the funeral facts`'s `the day of the fatal act`) LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the commencement of the Act`
    THEN `funeral not covered` `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
    ELSE IF NOT (    `the person who died was a primary victim of a homicide` `the funeral facts`
                 AND `the funeral facts`'s `the applicant has paid or is required to pay the funeral costs`)
         THEN `no funeral expense payment: not eligible, as the applicant has not paid and is not required to pay the funeral costs of a primary victim who died as a result of homicide (s 51)`
         ELSE IF NOT (`is on or before` (`the funeral facts`'s `the day of the funeral application`) (`the last day to apply for a funeral expense payment (s 54)` (`the funeral facts`'s `the day of the death`)))
              THEN `no funeral expense payment: the application is more than 3 years after the death, and the Act gives no power to extend that time (s 54)`
              ELSE IF `a disqualifying circumstance applies to a funeral application (ss 45, 60)` (`the funeral facts`'s `the conduct findings for the funeral application`)
                   THEN `no funeral expense payment: a disqualifying circumstance applies (ss 45 and 60)`
                   ELSE `a funeral expense payment of at most, in dollars`
                            (max 0 ((min (`the funeral facts`'s `the reasonable costs of the funeral`) `the reg s 11 maximum funeral expense payment`) MINUS (`the funeral facts`'s `associated payments covering the funeral costs`)))

§ `Part 5 -- repayment by the assisted person (ss 62 to 67)`

-- Dictionary: "associated payment" is "an amount, other than an amount received under this Act, that has been paid to
-- the applicant (or to another person for the applicant) as a result of an act of violence that is the subject of the
-- applicant's application", including damages, workers' compensation, an insurance payment and a reparation order.
-- It does not require the same harm or loss; only the s 62 repayment amount does.
-- s 62: "repayment amount ... means the lesser of (a) the amount of financial assistance and a funeral expense payment
-- made to the assisted person; and (b) the amount of the associated payment, or any part of the associated payment,
-- that covers the same harm or loss as an amount mentioned in paragraph (a) was intended to cover."
GIVEN `the assistance and funeral expense payment received` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the associated payment covering the same harm or loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the repayment amount (s 62)` `the assistance and funeral expense payment received` `the part of the associated payment covering the same harm or loss` MEANS
    min `the assistance and funeral expense payment received` `the part of the associated payment covering the same harm or loss`

-- s 64 (1): "This section applies if an assisted person receives an associated payment after any financial assistance or
-- funeral expense payment is made to the person." (2): "The assisted person must tell the commissioner, in writing,
-- about the associated payment within 28 days after the day the associated payment is received." (3): failing to is an
-- offence, "Maximum penalty: 50 penalty units, imprisonment for 6 months or both."
`the days to tell the commissioner about an associated payment (s 64 (2))` MEANS 28

DECLARE `Notification answer` IS ONE OF
    `must tell the commissioner in writing, by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `nothing to tell under s 64: it was received before any assistance was paid, so it may reduce the assistance instead (s 47 (1) (a))`
    `nothing to tell under s 64: it is not an associated payment, as it was not paid as a result of the act of violence`

GIVEN `paid as a result of the act of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `received after assistance was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notification answer`
`the s 64 answer for` `paid as a result of the act of violence` `received after assistance was paid` `the day it was received` MEANS
    IF NOT `paid as a result of the act of violence`
    THEN `nothing to tell under s 64: it is not an associated payment, as it was not paid as a result of the act of violence`
    ELSE IF NOT `received after assistance was paid`
         THEN `nothing to tell under s 64: it was received before any assistance was paid, so it may reduce the assistance instead (s 47 (1) (a))`
         ELSE `must tell the commissioner in writing, by` (`the days to tell the commissioner about an associated payment (s 64 (2))` `days after` `the day it was received`)

-- s 66 (2): "An assisted person who receives notice under subsection (1) must contact the commissioner within 28 days
-- after receiving the notice to enter an arrangement with the commissioner to ... (a) pay the repayment amount; (b) vary
-- the repayment amount." s 67 (2) (d): the repayment direction notice states "a date (the repayment date) that is at
-- least 28 days after the day the repayment direction notice is given".
`the days to contact the commissioner after a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (2))` MEANS 28
`the fewest days from a repayment direction notice to the repayment date (s 67 (2) (d))` MEANS 28

GIVEN `the day the notice was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to contact the commissioner after a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (2))` `the day the notice was received` MEANS
    `the days to contact the commissioner after a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (2))` `days after` `the day the notice was received`

-- s 65 (1): the section "applies if (a) an assisted person receives an associated payment after receiving financial
-- assistance or a funeral expense payment; and (b) the assisted person (i) is given a repayment direction notice; and
-- (ii) does not, on or before the repayment date stated in the notice, pay the repayment amount or apply for a review,
-- under section 67 (3) (b), of the repayment direction notice." (2), (3): the person is liable, and the amount "is a
-- debt due to the Territory". s 67 (4): an application for review "stays the assisted person's liability to pay";
-- (5): "dismissal of the assisted person's application for review removes the stay of liability". READING: after a
-- dismissal the person is liable, although s 65 (1) (b) (ii) is then not met in its terms (NOTES.md finding).
DECLARE `Repayment position` HAS
    `received the associated payment after the assistance`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been given a repayment direction notice`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid the repayment amount on or before the repayment date`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied to the ACAT for review on or before the repayment date`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ACAT dismissed the application for review`                     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Liability answer` IS ONE OF
    `not liable to repay under s 65: no associated payment after the assistance`
    `not liable to repay under s 65 unless given a repayment direction notice and the repayment date passes`
    `not liable: the repayment amount was paid by the repayment date`
    `liability stayed: an application to the ACAT for review was made by the repayment date (s 67 (4))`
    `liable: the ACAT dismissed the application for review, which removes the stay (s 67 (5))`
    `liable: the repayment amount is a debt due to the Territory (s 65 (2), (3))`

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Repayment position`
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
`the s 65 answer for` `the position` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the position`'s `received the associated payment after the assistance`)
    THEN `not liable to repay under s 65: no associated payment after the assistance`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the position`'s `has been given a repayment direction notice`)
         THEN `not liable to repay under s 65 unless given a repayment direction notice and the repayment date passes`
         ELSE IF `the position`'s `paid the repayment amount on or before the repayment date`
              THEN `not liable: the repayment amount was paid by the repayment date`
              ELSE IF `the position`'s `applied to the ACAT for review on or before the repayment date`
                   THEN IF `the position`'s `the ACAT dismissed the application for review`
                        THEN `liable: the ACAT dismissed the application for review, which removes the stay (s 67 (5))`
                        ELSE `liability stayed: an application to the ACAT for review was made by the repayment date (s 67 (4))`
                   ELSE `liable: the repayment amount is a debt due to the Territory (s 65 (2), (3))`

§ `Part 9 -- the deadline for reconsideration (s 92, schedule 2)`

-- Schedule 2, part 2.1 (internally reviewable) and part 2.2 (reviewable by the ACAT), for the applicant's decisions.
-- s 92 (1): an entity in part 2.1, column 4 "may apply to the commissioner for reconsideration"; (2): "within 28 days after
-- the day the notice of decision is given to the entity." s 95: an entity in part 2.2 may apply to the ACAT. s 67 (3) (b)
-- sets the time for the ACAT review of a repayment direction notice: on or before the repayment date.
DECLARE `Decision` IS ONE OF
    -- pt 2.1 item 1 and pt 2.2 item 1
    `not to extend the time for making an application (s 32)`
    -- pt 2.1 item 2 and pt 2.2 item 4
    `the amount of financial assistance (s 46)`
    -- pt 2.1 item 3 and pt 2.2 item 5
    `the amount of a reduction of financial assistance (s 47)`
    -- pt 2.1 item 4 and pt 2.2 item 6
    `the variation of an amount of financial assistance (s 50)`
    -- pt 2.1 item 5 and pt 2.2 item 7
    `the suspension of financial assistance (s 63)`
    -- pt 2.2 item 2 only
    `that applications involve related acts of violence (s 44)`
    -- pt 2.2 item 3 only
    `that financial assistance is not to be given (s 45)`
    -- pt 2.2 item 8 only
    `a requirement to repay financial assistance (s 67)`

`the days to apply for reconsideration (s 92 (2))` MEANS 28

DECLARE `Review answer` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the commissioner for reconsideration, in writing with the grounds, by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `apply to the ACAT for review on or before the repayment date in the repayment direction notice (s 67 (3) (b))`
    `review not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision`
      `the day the notice of decision was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Review answer`
`the review answer for` `the decision` `the day the notice of decision was given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `that applications involve related acts of violence (s 44)` THEN `review not covered` `review by the ACAT (part 9, s 95): its procedure and time limit are in the ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2008, which is not deposited`
    WHEN `that financial assistance is not to be given (s 45)` THEN `review not covered` `review by the ACAT (part 9, s 95): its procedure and time limit are in the ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2008, which is not deposited`
    WHEN `a requirement to repay financial assistance (s 67)` THEN `apply to the ACAT for review on or before the repayment date in the repayment direction notice (s 67 (3) (b))`
    OTHERWISE `apply to the commissioner for reconsideration, in writing with the grounds, by` (`the days to apply for reconsideration (s 92 (2))` `days after` `the day the notice of decision was given`)

§ `Part 10 -- lawyers' legal costs (s 96, reg s 12)`

-- s 96 (1): "A lawyer must not charge or seek to recover legal costs that are higher than the amount prescribed by
-- regulation for the following: (a) legal services that relate to an application for financial assistance; (b) legal
-- services that relate to an appeal or review process under this Act." Reg s 12: "(1) ... $1 455. (2) ... $2 910."
-- The s 97 WPI indexation is taken as reflected in R11.
DECLARE `Legal services` IS ONE OF
    `legal services for an application for financial assistance`
    `legal services for an appeal or review process under the Act`

GIVEN `the services` IS A `Legal services`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a lawyer may charge for` `the services` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the services`
    WHEN `legal services for an application for financial assistance` THEN 1455
    WHEN `legal services for an appeal or review process under the Act` THEN 2910

§ `Not covered`

DECLARE `Other topic` IS ONE OF
    `recovering the assistance from the offender (part 6)`
    `the levy on convicted offenders (part 7)`
    `the commissioner's administration, and the secrecy of my information (part 8)`
    `how the ACAT reviews a decision (part 9)`
    `an application about a criminal injury before 1 July 2016 (s 98)`
    `what the commissioner's guidelines say (s 87)`

DECLARE `Coverage answer` IS ONE OF
    `not covered by this encoding` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the topic` IS AN `Other topic`
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`the coverage answer for` `the topic` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the topic`
    WHEN `recovering the assistance from the offender (part 6)` THEN `not covered by this encoding` `recovery from the offender (part 6) is not encoded`
    WHEN `the levy on convicted offenders (part 7)` THEN `not covered by this encoding` `the victims financial assistance levy on convicted offenders (part 7) is not encoded`
    WHEN `the commissioner's administration, and the secrecy of my information (part 8)` THEN `not covered by this encoding` `administration, the commissioner's functions and secrecy (part 8) are not encoded`
    WHEN `how the ACAT reviews a decision (part 9)` THEN `not covered by this encoding` `review by the ACAT (part 9, s 95): its procedure and time limit are in the ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2008, which is not deposited`
    WHEN `an application about a criminal injury before 1 July 2016 (s 98)` THEN `not covered by this encoding` `an act of violence before 1 July 2016: applications for criminal injuries before the Act (s 98) are not encoded`
    WHEN `what the commissioner's guidelines say (s 87)` THEN `not covered by this encoding` `the commissioner's guidelines (s 87) are not deposited`

§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant, the assisted person, the commissioner and the applicant's lawyer`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule starts. The commissioner is a party only for what the applicant is owed.
DECLARE `VOC party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the assisted person`
    `the commissioner`
    `the applicant's lawyer`

DECLARE `Repayment response` IS ONE OF
    `by contacting the commissioner to arrange to pay or vary the repayment amount`
    `by paying the repayment amount`

DECLARE `Direction response` IS ONE OF
    `by paying the commissioner the repayment amount`
    `by applying to the ACAT for review of the repayment direction notice`

DECLARE `VOC act` IS ONE OF
    `apply for financial assistance` HAS `meets s 31 (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `give the applicant written notice about repayment and recovery (s 33)`
    `extend the time for making the application (s 32 (2))`
    `give the applicant written notice of the apparent disqualifying circumstance (s 45 (2))`
    `tell the commissioner in writing why the disqualifying circumstance does not apply`
    `decide whether a disqualifying circumstance applies, and tell the applicant (s 45 (3))`
    `give the applicant financial assistance`
    `apply for a funeral expense payment` HAS `meets s 52` IS A BOOLEAN
    `give the applicant written notice about repayment and recovery (s 55)`
    `tell the commissioner in writing about the associated payment`
    `give the assisted person a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (1))`
    `respond to the repayment arrangement notice` HAS `how` IS A `Repayment response`
    `give the assisted person a repayment direction notice (s 67 (2))`
    `respond to the repayment direction notice` HAS `how` IS A `Direction response`
    `charge or seek to recover legal costs of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- s 33 (1): "As soon as practicable after the day the commissioner receives an application ... the commissioner must
-- give the applicant written notice about the action that may be taken against (a) an applicant under part 5 ...; and
-- (b) an offender under part 6". No number of days: no WITHIN, so it never becomes a breach by time alone.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 33 -- the commissioner must give notice about repayment and recovery` IS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `give the applicant written notice about repayment and recovery (s 33)`

-- s 31 (1): "A person (the applicant) may apply to the commissioner for financial assistance." s 32 (1): within 3 years
-- (the days to the last day are the input); s 32 (2): the commissioner may extend the time. Applying is a choice (DO);
-- only an application that meets s 31 (2) counts. After the deadline, only an extension opens the way again.
GIVEN `days to the last day to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `ss 31 to 33 -- the applicant may apply within 3 years, or later if the commissioner extends the time` IS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    DO     `apply for financial assistance` `complies` PROVIDED `complies`
    WITHIN `days to the last day to apply`
    HENCE  `s 33 -- the commissioner must give notice about repayment and recovery`
    LEST
        PARTY `the commissioner`
        MAY   `extend the time for making the application (s 32 (2))`
        HENCE
            PARTY `the applicant`
            DO    `apply for financial assistance` `complies after the extension` PROVIDED `complies after the extension`
            HENCE `s 33 -- the commissioner must give notice about repayment and recovery`

-- s 45 (2): the commissioner "must give the applicant written notice (a) stating that the application ... appears to
-- involve a disqualifying circumstance ...; and (b) asking the applicant to tell the commissioner, in writing, within
-- 14 days after the notice is received, if there is a reason why the disqualifying circumstance does not apply."
-- (3): after considering any reasons, the commissioner must decide and tell the applicant. (4): if a disqualifying
-- circumstance applies, "the commissioner must not give financial assistance". Answering is a choice (MAY): either way,
-- the decision follows. The prohibition has no end date, so it is checked with #TRACE.
GIVEN `the commissioner decides that a disqualifying circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 45 (3), (4) -- the commissioner decides, and must not give assistance if a disqualifying circumstance applies` IS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `decide whether a disqualifying circumstance applies, and tell the applicant (s 45 (3))`
    HENCE
        IF `the commissioner decides that a disqualifying circumstance applies`
        THEN PARTY `the commissioner`
             SHANT `give the applicant financial assistance`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the commissioner` BECAUSE "s 45 (4): the commissioner decided that a disqualifying circumstance applies, so must not give financial assistance"
        ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `the commissioner decides that a disqualifying circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 45 -- notice of a disqualifying circumstance, 14 days to answer, then the decision` IS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `give the applicant written notice of the apparent disqualifying circumstance (s 45 (2))`
    HENCE
        PARTY  `the applicant`
        MAY    `tell the commissioner in writing why the disqualifying circumstance does not apply`
        WITHIN `the days to answer a notice of a disqualifying circumstance (s 45 (2) (b))`
        HENCE  `s 45 (3), (4) -- the commissioner decides, and must not give assistance if a disqualifying circumstance applies` `the commissioner decides that a disqualifying circumstance applies`

-- s 52: a funeral application must be in writing, with a contact address and anything the regulation prescribes (R11
-- prescribes nothing). s 54: within 3 years after the death (the days to the last day are the input), with no power to
-- extend. s 55: the commissioner must give the s 33-style notice. Missing the deadline is no breach: the right is gone.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 55 -- the commissioner must give notice about repayment and recovery` IS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `give the applicant written notice about repayment and recovery (s 55)`

-- (The commissioner's notice is a named rule so that the LEST below attaches to the applicant's rule, not to it.)
GIVEN `days to the last day to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `ss 52, 54, 55 -- the applicant may apply for a funeral expense payment within 3 years after the death` IS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    DO     `apply for a funeral expense payment` `complies` PROVIDED `complies`
    WITHIN `days to the last day to apply`
    HENCE  `s 55 -- the commissioner must give notice about repayment and recovery`
    LEST   FULFILLED

-- s 67 (3): "An assisted person who is given notice under subsection (2) must, on or before the repayment date (a) pay
-- the commissioner the repayment amount; or (b) apply to the ACAT for review of the repayment direction notice."
-- s 65: otherwise the repayment amount is a debt due to the Territory.
GIVEN `days from the direction notice to the repayment date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 67 -- after a repayment direction notice, pay or apply for review by the repayment date` IS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `give the assisted person a repayment direction notice (s 67 (2))`
    HENCE
        PARTY  `the assisted person`
        MUST   `respond to the repayment direction notice` `how`
        WITHIN `days from the direction notice to the repayment date`
        LEST   BREACH BY `the assisted person` BECAUSE "s 65, s 67 (3): the repayment amount was neither paid nor put to ACAT review by the repayment date, so it is a debt due to the Territory"

-- s 66 (1): "As soon as practicable after receiving information under section 64 (2) the commissioner must give the
-- assisted person written notice (a repayment arrangement notice)". (2): the assisted person "must contact the
-- commissioner within 28 days after receiving the notice to enter an arrangement ... to (a) pay the repayment amount;
-- (b) vary the repayment amount." s 67 (1): if the person has not within 28 days "(i) made contact with the
-- commissioner; or (ii) paid the repayment amount", the commissioner must give a repayment direction notice.
GIVEN `days from the direction notice to the repayment date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `ss 66, 67 -- the repayment arrangement notice, then a direction notice if there is no contact within 28 days` IS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `give the assisted person a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (1))`
    HENCE
        PARTY  `the assisted person`
        MUST   `respond to the repayment arrangement notice` `how`
        WITHIN `the days to contact the commissioner after a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (2))`
        LEST   `s 67 -- after a repayment direction notice, pay or apply for review by the repayment date` `days from the direction notice to the repayment date`

-- s 64 (2), (3): within 28 days after receiving an associated payment that comes after the assistance; then s 66.
GIVEN `received after the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the direction notice to the repayment date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 64 -- the assisted person must tell the commissioner about an associated payment within 28 days` IS
    IF `received after the assistance`
    THEN PARTY  `the assisted person`
         MUST   `tell the commissioner in writing about the associated payment`
         WITHIN `the days to tell the commissioner about an associated payment (s 64 (2))`
         HENCE  `ss 66, 67 -- the repayment arrangement notice, then a direction notice if there is no contact within 28 days` `days from the direction notice to the repayment date`
         LEST   BREACH BY `the assisted person` BECAUSE "s 64 (2), (3): an assisted person who fails to tell the commissioner about an associated payment within 28 days commits an offence (maximum 50 penalty units, imprisonment for 6 months or both)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 96 (1): "A lawyer must not charge or seek to recover legal costs that are higher than the amount prescribed".
-- Only a charge above the limit counts. No end date: checked with #TRACE.
GIVEN `the services` IS A `Legal services`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOC party` `VOC act`
DECIDE `s 96 -- the applicant's lawyer must not charge more than the prescribed legal costs` IS
    PARTY `the applicant's lawyer`
    SHANT `charge or seek to recover legal costs of` `the amount` PROVIDED `the amount` GREATER THAN `the most a lawyer may charge for` `the services`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant's lawyer` BECAUSE "s 96 (1), reg s 12: a lawyer must not charge or seek to recover legal costs above $1 455 for an application, or $2 910 for an appeal or review"
